  "notes": "Synthetic. Truth is what each line actually does at run time. The engine resolves within one file in v0, so the client built by app/factory.py:make_client and the constant in app/settings.py are reported as gaps at their use sites (dynamic.py:34 and :21) and recorded here as known misses. dynamic.py:38 receives an untyped parameter that nothing in the fixture calls, so its provider is not knowable and it is a gap only. app/sms.py (Twilio messages.create) and app/pricing.py (model IDs in a price table) must report nothing. venv/ and libs/_vendor/ hold one SDK call each and must be excluded and counted. app/dynamic.py:13 reads OPENAI_MODEL with a literal fallback: the fallback is captured as env_default and the call keeps its env_var gap. app/secrets_review.py holds the five leaks from the review of #276; each refused model is an unresolved_model gap with reason credential and no secret may reach the output. app/recall.py:38 resolves `llm` because run() is the only in-file caller of send() and passes the module client, and keeps an ambiguous_client gap (in_file_callers) because send() is public and other modules may pass another client; :47 is custom_base_url because with_options was given a base_url. bin/summarize has no extension and is scanned for its Python shebang; .github/scripts/triage.py is counted under skipped.hidden_*."
